scope: |
  First of the ARCH-3 splits. DispatchRuntime.infix2 is 21114 bytecodes — 2.6x over HotSpot's
  HugeMethodLimit — so it is NEVER JIT-compiled, and every INT method call goes through it.
  Split the op-groups into helpers so the dispatcher lands under the limit, then measure with an
  ALTERNATING A/B (one run on a loaded host manufactures numbers). Land only if the measurement
  supports it; revert if not. BUGS §v1-interpreter-hot-path-never-jits.
  NOT taking F4: v2/lib is held by the LIVE v2-backend-matrix-gaps claim (commit 56 s ago).
next: baseline census + bench, split, verify conformance, alternating A/B, update the frozen list
